module gunbc.roadmap.attempt_system_unit_launch

// SYSTEM-MANAGER TRANSIENT ATTEMPT UNITS, via a narrow privileged launcher. srv1's user manager
// drops ProtectSystem/ProtectHome/ReadWritePaths (apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1). PID 1
// enforces them. The privileged effect is: start ONE transient system unit named
// gunbc-attempt-<node>-<key>.service, User= the instance service user, properties from the same
// typed confinement fold, ExecStart the request's argv on the instance binary. Which authorization pattern performs
// that effect is gunbc.auth.authorization_pattern_selection, not a call-site choice.
//
// THE GRANT IS THE LAUNCHER ARGV. Belt does not sudo systemd-run with caller-chosen -p flags.
// sudoers matches one exact `gunbc run` of attempt_system_unit_launch_cli with --arg instance_root
// pinned. DESIGN §3 replacement: no --user dual path.
//
// THE REQUEST NAMES AN ATTEMPT; ROOT DERIVES EVERYTHING PRIVILEGED (review 80324). Each request is
// one create-only directory named from (node id, attempt key), staged then renamed into `requests/`.
// It carries only the attempt's identity, the memory grant and the worker argv. User=, the working
// directory, the writable worktree and log paths and the ExecStopPost exit hook are derived here
// from the instance and that identity, with the same functions the belt plans with. A request cannot
// name a `+`-prefixed exit hook (which systemd runs with full privileges) or widen ReadWritePaths:
// those fields do not exist in it. The launcher claims by rename into `claimed/` (requester cannot
// write that directory) and writes `answers/<entry>`. Two overlapping sudo launches cannot share one
// body; a second write for the same attempt refuses (review 80347).
//
// ONE SUDOERS FILE PER INSTANCE, installed only by that instance's deploy
// (`/etc/sudoers.d/gunbc-attempt-system-unit-<instance_id>`). A host-global file that named both
// srv1-live and srv1-lab meant a lab deploy installed production's grant.
//
// THE BYTES ROOT RUNS ARE A ROOT-OWNED RELEASE, not the instance checkout. The grant names
// /opt/gunbc/attempt-system-unit-helpers/<instance_id>/<sha>/{gunbc,dag,src/v2}, installed by that
// instance's deploy the same way approval-broker-helpers are: root-owned, not group- or
// world-writable, sha-addressed, sudoers pinned to that path. The requester can edit
// instance.serve_binary and the checkout; those paths are not the grant.

